SUMMARY:Applied Mathematics Seminar: Kirill Golubnichiy — A Semi-Discrete
  Convexification Method Combined with Deep Learning for Electrical Impedan
 ce Tomography
DESCRIPTION:Kirill Golubnichiy\, Texas Tech University\nA Semi-Discrete Con
 vexification Method Combined with Deep Learning for Electrical Impedance T
 omography\nIn this talk\, we develop a new semi-discrete version of the Ca
 rleman estimate-based convexification method\, a globally convergent numer
 ical approach for nonlinear inverse problems. The semi-discrete convexific
 ation method is used to generate an accurate starting point for the subseq
 uent deep learning training procedure. An important feature of the continu
 ous convexification method is that its convergence to the true solution do
 es not require the availability of a sufficiently accurate initial guess.\
 n\nWe introduce a new concept of (h)-strong convexity\, where (h) denotes 
 the grid step size in the semi-discrete formulation. This property enables
  us to derive an a priori accuracy estimate for the starting point supplie
 d to the deep learning stage. The proposed approach is applied to the high
 ly nonlinear inverse problem of Electrical Impedance Tomography. Numerical
  experiments involving complicated conductivity structures demonstrate the
  accuracy\, robustness\, and computational feasibility of the combined sem
 i-discrete convexification and deep learning procedure.\nhttps://jiazhaoma
 th.github.io/seminar/2026-2027.html#2026-11-20
URL:https://jiazhaomath.github.io/seminar/2026-2027.html#2026-11-20
END:VEVENT
